WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.607
Python uses zero-based indexing, so the first value is at position zero.

00:00:05.607 --> 00:00:11.487
Scores zero returns eighty-two. Scores one returns seventy-six.

00:00:11.487 --> 00:00:15.872
A negative one means the last value, which is sixty-nine.

00:00:15.872 --> 00:00:19.507
A slice lets us retrieve several values.

00:00:19.507 --> 00:00:26.877
Scores one through four starts at index one and stops before index four, giving seventy-six, ninety-one,

00:00:26.877 --> 00:00:28.966
and eighty-eight.

00:00:29.772 --> 00:00:31.704
The stop position is excluded.

00:00:31.704 --> 00:00:36.644
That detail appears throughout Python, so it is worth getting comfortable with early.
